{"parentUuid":"63b9f885-d35c-4880-99f4-cb9fa097835c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CaP2rVY43KDFN2nuukX4qG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For 99% of users, **nothing changes**. The fix is invisible on the happy path — successful reviews look identical to how they look today.\n\nThe change is only visible when something silently fails. Concretely:\n\n**Today, when the manifest write skips (your 12:36 case):**\n\n```\ncodex                 ✓ done      7m40s\n\n2 agent(s) done — 2 succeeded, 0 failed, 0 cancelled\nGenerating summary...\n\n  ## Unified Review Verdict\n  ...\n\n[end of output — that's it]\n```\n\nYou see the review output, the synthesis, and then nothing. No error, no warning, no hint that anything went wrong. You only discover the failure later when `entire review --findings` says nothing's there.\n\n**After the fix, same scenario:**\n\n```\ncodex                 ✓ done      7m40s\n\n2 agent(s) done — 2 succeeded, 0 failed, 0 cancelled\nGenerating summary...\n\n  ## Unified Review Verdict\n  ...\n\nNote: review skills ran successfully but findings were not persisted.\n  Reason: review session was not tagged as a review (env-var handshake did not reach the hook)\n  `entire review --findings` and `entire review --fix` will not see this run.\n  Re-run with `ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL=debug` for diagnostic detail.\n```\n\nSame agent output, same synthesis — but instead of trailing off into nothing, the user gets four lines telling them exactly what happened, what won't work as a result, and how to dig deeper.\n\n**On the happy path (today's working case from a fresh terminal):**\n\nNothing changes. The \"Review complete. To apply all review findings: ...\" footer prints exactly as it does now. The only difference is that the code path leading up to it has one extra branch that *would* print the warning if `Sources == 0`, but on a working run that branch never fires.\n\n**Debug log change (lifecycle.go:1042):**\n\nInvisible to users entirely unless they explicitly set `ENTIRE_LOG_LEVEL=debug`. Even then it only adds one line per non-review turn to the log file (which lives at `.entire/logs/`). Users running normally never see it.\n\nSo the user-visible surface is exactly: *one warning block in the failure case, zero changes on the happy path*. That's the whole UX delta. The rest of the PR (debug logs, helper function, tests) is plumbing that makes the failure case diagnosable but doesn't change what users see.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- This is the right shape for a silent-failure fix: zero noise added to the success path, useful information added to the failure path. The mistake to avoid is the opposite shape — adding \"for your information\" output to the happy path \"in case something goes wrong,\" which is what produces the dreaded warning-spam-everyone-ignores problem. The user should never see new output unless something actually failed.\n- The exact wording of the warning matters more than its existence. \"Reason: review session was not tagged as a review (env-var handshake did not reach the hook)\" is jargon-heavy and assumes context the user doesn't have. Real-world v2 of this would probably soften it: \"Reason: a setup step didn't complete; agents ran but their output won't be retrievable later.\" Less precise, but understandable to the median user. Worth iterating on copy with someone less in-the-weeds than us — e.g., paste both versions to a coworker who didn't follow this thread and see which one actually communicates.\n- One thing notably absent from this PR: any attempt to recover. The warning tells the user \"this run won't be visible to --findings\" but doesn't offer to retry, save the agent output to a file as a consolation prize, or let them attach the run via `entire review attach <session-id>`. There's a reasonable v2 conversation about whether the warning should also write the agent narratives to a fallback file (`.git/entire-review/orphans/<timestamp>.txt`) so the work isn't fully lost. But that adds complexity, and the v1 fix should ship first — recovery is a separate design question.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5085,"cache_read_input_tokens":179283,"output_tokens":1759,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5085,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1759,"cache_read_input_tokens":179283,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5085},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaqbPcQW5L4N7DZFWqK2Q","type":"assistant","uuid":"ebb9b5c7-6e9d-4825-a7c2-c49f19ae75e3","timestamp":"2026-05-08T18:43:08.272Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli","sessionId":"802b09ab-4617-4518-902c-87ed5837e8f3","version":"2.1.133","gitBranch":"main"}
